# This directory must EXIST for the app to import at all.
#
# main.py mounts it unconditionally: StaticFiles(directory="public") raises
# RuntimeError at import time when the directory is missing, which takes down
# create_app() — and with it the 15 tests in test_app_assembly.py, where BOTH
# MODULE_MAP anti-drift assertions live (every live route resolves to exactly
# one policy; every table key still matches a route). Those are the guardrails
# that would catch a mis-classified path or the "*" sentinel leaking into
# MODULE_KEYS, so losing them to an import error is the worst way to lose them:
# the suite reports errors, not failures, and a fresh worktree looks broken
# rather than unguarded.
#
# Git does not track empty directories, and the only real file here
# (Favicon-01.svg) is not committed — so without this placeholder every clean
# clone and every git worktree starts out in that state. It did, once.
